# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Walls that are not their box (bim_ifc_native.dl): a gable wall given as
# a faceted B-rep, with a door cut from its foot, becomes a native wall
# with the gable as the outline of its face and the door as its opening;
# a wall under a lean-to roof with a step in its foot takes that outline
# too. Both evaluate to the volume the file gives them (the gable's less
# its door's rough opening). A wall with an overhang has no foot and top
# line of one height each: it stays an imported element. A wall that starts
# under its storey keeps its windows with their sill under the storey, two
# side by side as one opening; a cut from a wall's foot that nothing fills
# is a step in its outline, no opening. The outline is kept to the
# millimetre: a wall a nanometre longer than its outline evaluates too.
import ifc/bim_ifc_native.dl
import elements/planar/bim_evaluate.dl
import ui/editor/bim_editor.dl

set ifcLines to an empty list of a string
append (the string form of "ISO-10303-21;") to ifcLines
append (the string form of "HEADER;") to ifcLines
append (the string form of "FILE_DESCRIPTION(('ViewDefinition [ReferenceView]'),'2;1');") to ifcLines
